# The database is .issues/*.md and the file format is the API, so the bytes are
# part of it. ISS-033 made every write LF; core.autocrlf is `true` on the
# machine this repo is developed on, which was converting them straight back on
# checkout - the CRLF was never in the index, git was putting it in the working
# tree. Without this line the normalise pass that closed ISS-033 is undone by
# the next `git checkout` and `issue check` starts failing again on thirty-five
# files nobody touched.
#
# Scoped to what the tool writes - which now includes the event logs, whose
# first committed file lands with ISS-039. `append_event` writes LF and
# json.loads tolerates a stray carriage return, so there is no bug attached
# to that one - only the same diff on every line of a file nobody touched. The .py sources
# have that churn too and keep whatever the clone decides.
.issues/**/*.md text eol=lf
.issues/**/*.jsonl text eol=lf
